 (lucide) |         |","table":"table-3"},"436":{"id":"/docs/components/button#53","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#roundbutton","content":"| Prop                 | Type                                       | Default |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------- |\n| `accessibilityLabel` | `string` (required: an icon names nothing) |         |","table":"table-3"},"437":{"id":"/docs/components/button#54","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#roundbutton","content":"| Prop       | Type          | Default |\n| ---------- | ------------- | ------- |\n| `children` | `JSX.Element` |         |","table":"table-3"},"438":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"page","content":"Calendar","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar"},"439":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#0","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar","content":"A month of days to pick a date or a range, on the shared calendar look."},"440":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#1","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#installation","content":"Installation"},"441":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#2","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#usage","content":"Usage"},"442":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#3","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#examples","content":"Examples"},"443":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#4","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"444":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#5","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#uncontrolled","content":"Uncontrolled"},"445":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#6","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#api","content":"API"},"446":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#7","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"447":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#8","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#controlled","content":"`value` is an ISO date; with `range` it is `[start, end]`. While the second end is chosen, the band\npreviews the range from the first to a later day under the pointer or the keyboard; the pick\ncommits it. A day before the first starts the range again, so nothing is previewed there."},"448":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#9","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#uncontrolled","content":"Without `value` the calendar keeps its own, starting at `defaultValue`."},"449":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#10","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#api","content":"Defaults from `calendarLook` / `CalendarItem`. Every prop of `nsh/base` Calendar passes through."},"450":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#11","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#api","content":"| Part       | Props                                        | Description                                                             |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Calendar` | `value`, `defaultValue`, `onChange`, `range` | A month of days to pick a date or a range, on the shared calendar look. |","table":"table-0"},"451":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar#12","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#api","content":"| Part           | Props                                                  | Description                                                                            |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CalendarItem` | `item` (a `CalendarEntry`), `months`, `firstDayOfWeek` | One day of the grid (a square in `shape.control`); what `renderItem` draws by default. |","table":"table-0"},"452":{"id":"/docs/components/card","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"page","content":"Card","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card"},"453":{"id":"/docs/components/card#0","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"A flat surface that groups related content: a header with its action, a body and a footer."},"454":{"id":"/docs/components/card#1","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#installation","content":"Installation"},"455":{"id":"/docs/components/card#2","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#usage","content":"Usage"},"456":{"id":"/docs/components/card#3","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#composition","content":"Composition"},"457":{"id":"/docs/components/card#4","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#examples","content":"Examples"},"458":{"id":"/docs/components/card#5","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#with-a-form","content":"With a form"},"459":{"id":"/docs/components/card#6","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#two-side-by-side","content":"Two side by side"},"460":{"id":"/docs/components/card#7","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#a-footer-that-wraps","content":"A footer that wraps"},"461":{"id":"/docs/components/card#8","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#flush","content":"Flush"},"462":{"id":"/docs/components/card#9","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"API"},"463":{"id":"/docs/components/card#10","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"464":{"id":"/docs/components/card#11","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#composition","content":"Use the following composition to build a `Card`:"},"465":{"id":"/docs/components/card#12","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#with-a-form","content":"`CardContent` pads its sides and nothing else: space the fields the way the form needs."},"466":{"id":"/docs/components/card#13","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#two-side-by-side","content":"A card takes the width its style gives it; `flexGrow` with `flexBasis` puts two across a window\nand one across a phone."},"467":{"id":"/docs/components/card#14","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#a-footer-that-wraps","content":"`CardFooter` is a row that wraps: a long pair of buttons goes to two lines on a phone rather than\nsqueezing both."},"468":{"id":"/docs/components/card#15","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#flush","content":"`flush` on `CardContent` drops the side padding and pulls the body through the card's bottom padding, so a picture meets the rim. The card's `overflow: hidden` clips it to the radius. The header stays padded. Off in the terminal."},"469":{"id":"/docs/components/card#16","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"Each part is the `nsh` element it is drawn with. Every view prop passes through; `style` goes over\nthe part's own."},"470":{"id":"/docs/components/card#17","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"| Part   | Props | Description                               |\n| ------ | ----- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `Card` | —     | The flat surface holding related content. |","table":"table-0"},"471":{"id":"/docs/components/card#18","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"| Part         | Props | Description                                                                  |\n| ------------ | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CardHeader` | —     | Title over description in the first column, the action at the trailing edge. |","table":"table-0"},"472":{"id":"/docs/components/card#19","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"| Part        | Props | Description                                         |\n| ----------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CardTitle` | —     | A step larger than body, semibold, the text colour. |","table":"table-0"},"473":{"id":"/docs/components/card#20","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"| Part              | Props | Description                    |\n| ----------------- | ----- | ------------------------------ |\n| `CardDescription` | —     | Body size in the muted colour. |","table":"table-0"},"474":{"id":"/docs/components/card#21","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"| Part         | Props | Description                                                     |\n| ------------ | ----- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CardAction` | —     | The control at the trailing edge, beside title and description. |","table":"table-0"},"475":{"id":"/docs/components/card#22","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"| Part          | Props   | Description                                                             |\n| ------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CardContent` | `flush` | What the card is about. `flush` meets the card's side and bottom edges. |","table":"table-0"},"476":{"id":"/docs/components/card#23","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"| Part         | Props | Description                       |\n| ------------ | ----- | --------------------------------- |\n| `CardFooter` | —     | A wrapping row, centred, 8 apart. |","table":"table-0"},"477":{"id":"/docs/components/card#24","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#api","content":"`CardTitle` and `CardDescription` are `Text`, so they take text props (`numberOfLines`, `role`).\n`CardHeader` is a grid of two columns: the title over the description in the first and the action\nat the trailing edge of the first row, whichever order the three are written in."},"478":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"page","content":"Carousel","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel"},"479":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#0","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel","content":"Snapping slides with arrows and a traveling dot pill."},"480":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#1","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#installation","content":"Installation"},"481":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#2","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#usage","content":"Usage"},"482":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#3","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#composition","content":"Composition"},"483":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#4","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#examples","content":"Examples"},"484":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#5","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#slides","content":"Slides"},"485":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#6","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#caption-over-a-photo","content":"Caption over a photo"},"486":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#7","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#arrows","content":"Arrows"},"487":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#8","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#pagination","content":"Pagination"},"488":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#9","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#autoplay","content":"Autoplay"},"489":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#10","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"API"},"490":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#11","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"491":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#12","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#composition","content":"Use the following composition to build a `Carousel`:"},"492":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#13","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#caption-over-a-photo","content":"A slide that holds a photograph draws its caption itself: the theme has no text role that reads\nover an arbitrary picture, so the ink is `on-media` (white in every theme, both appearances) and\nthe veil behind it is `scrim`. A text role such as `foreground` flips with the appearance and\nleaves the caption unreadable in one of them."},"493":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#14","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#arrows","content":"`CarouselPrevious` and `CarouselNext` draw their own icon and size; `side` and `glass` change the\nchrome. Under every theme they are the same floating pill beside the dots; `carouselArrowLook()`\nhas no per-theme form to follow."},"494":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#15","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#pagination","content":"The indicator travels to `index`; each item shows the `CarouselDot` you give it. The carousel keeps\nthe slide shown to itself (`nsh/base` only reports it through `onChange`), so an item with no child\ndraws nothing: pass the dot, and tell it which slide it is on."},"495":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#16","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#autoplay","content":"The carousel holds no timer: a slide that moves on by itself is the app's — a controlled `index` a\ntimer advances, around the ends. Hold it while the user is at the carousel: the pointer over a\n`View` around it (`onMouseEnter` / `onMouseLeave`), the keyboard focus in it (`onFocus` /\n`onBlur`) and a drag (`onDragStart` / `onDragEnd`), and leave it off with `reduceMotion()`. Key the\neffect on the index, so every change — a timer's, an arrow's, a dot's, the rotation control's —\nstarts a whole interval, or a press would be cut short by the turn already under way. The rotation\ncontrol comes first in the row, beside the dots, and names itself `Pause announcements` or\n`Play announcements`."},"496":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#17","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"Uses `carouselArrowLook`, `carouselPaginationLook`, `carouselDotItemLook`, and `CarouselDot`. `carouselArrowLook()`'s `icon` is the glyph an arrow draws and its `style` / `hoverStyle` / `activeStyle` / `focusVisibleStyle` are the arrow's chrome. Every prop of `nsh/base` Carousel parts passes through."},"497":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#18","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"| Part       | Props | Description                            |\n| ---------- | ----- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `Carousel` | —     | The carousel over `nsh/base` Carousel. |","table":"table-0"},"498":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#19","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"| Part              | Props | Description                             |\n| ----------------- | ----- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `CarouselContent` | —     | The snap viewport the slides scroll in. |","table":"table-0"},"499":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#20","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"| Part           | Props | Description                                              |\n| -------------- | ----- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CarouselItem` | —     | One slide: one per view unless the app gives it a width. |","table":"table-0"},"500":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#21","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"| Part               | Props           | Description                                                                       |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CarouselPrevious` | `glass`, `side` | The arrow back: `glass` and `side` shape its look, an arrow unless given a child. |","table":"table-0"},"501":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#22","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"| Part           | Props           | Description                             |\n| -------------- | --------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `CarouselNext` | `glass`, `side` | The arrow forward, as the previous one. |","table":"table-0"},"502":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#23","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"| Part                 | Props | Description                                                 |\n| -------------------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CarouselPagination` | —     | The dot row, with the pill that travels to the slide shown. |","table":"table-0"},"503":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#24","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"| Part                     | Props                                             | Description                                    |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `CarouselPaginationItem` | `children` (a `CarouselDot`; nothing without one) | One slide's dot, named `Slide 1`, `Slide 2`, … |","table":"table-0"},"504":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel#25","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel#api","content":"| Part          | Props      | Description                                                                                  |\n| ------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CarouselDot` | `selected` | A quiet circle that brightens under the pointer and hides under the pill on the slide shown. |","table":"table-0"},"505":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"page","content":"Checkbox","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox"},"506":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#0","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox","content":"A sunk box that fills in citrus, with a check or a dash springing in."},"507":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#1","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#installation","content":"Installation"},"508":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#2","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#usage","content":"Usage"},"509":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#3","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#examples","content":"Examples"},"510":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#4","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#size","content":"Size"},"511":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#5","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"512":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#6","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#round","content":"Round"},"513":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#7","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#checked-and-indeterminate","content":"Checked and indeterminate"},"514":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#8","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#names-for-screen-readers","content":"Names for screen readers"},"515":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#9","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/checkbox#api","content":"API"},"516":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#10","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"517":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#11","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox#size","content":"`size` multiplies the page's control size: `sm` 0.8, `default` 1, `lg` 1.25 (`ChoiceSize`)."},"518":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#12","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox#names-for-screen-readers","content":"A string child is the row's label and its name for screen readers, so the box and its text are one control to a reader; `accessibilityLabel` wins when it should differ. Children drawn as given are named by the texts inside them."},"519":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#13","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox#api","content":"Every prop of `nsh/base` Checkbox passes through. `indicatorClass` and `indicatorStyle` go over the look's. The row is the `group` the box sinks with while pressed."},"520":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#14","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox#api","content":"| Part       | Props                                                                                                      | Description                                                                                         |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Checkbox` | `size`: `ChoiceSize` (default `\"default\"`), `round` (default `false`), `children`: `string \\| JSX.Element` | The box of the theme's choice recipe, filling as it is checked; the row is the group it sinks with. |","table":"table-0"},"521":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#15","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox#api","content":"| Part           | Props                                                 | Description                                                               |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CheckboxMark` | `mark`: `\"check\" \\| \"dash\" \\| null`, `scale`, `round` | The check or the dash that springs in, drawn into the look's `indicator`. |","table":"table-0"},"522":{"id":"/docs/components/checkbox#16","page_id":"/docs/components/checkbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/checkbox#api","content":"`ChoiceSize` is `\"sm\" | \"default\" | \"lg\"`: 0.8, 1 or 1.25 times the page's control size, shared with `Radio`. The table is `choiceScales` in `lib/choice`."},"523":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"page","content":"CodeBlock","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block"},"524":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#0","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block","content":"Code, a command's output or a log in a block, with a title, a copy button, line numbers and a footer."},"525":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#1","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#installation","content":"Installation"},"526":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#2","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#usage","content":"Usage"},"527":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#3","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#composition","content":"Composition"},"528":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#4","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#examples","content":"Examples"},"529":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#5","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#variant","content":"Variant"},"530":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#6","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#size","content":"Size"},"531":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#7","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#header-and-copy","content":"Header and copy"},"532":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#8","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#line-numbers","content":"Line numbers"},"533":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#9","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#lines-of-your-own","content":"Lines of your own"},"534":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#10","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#footer","content":"Footer"},"535":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#11","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#height","content":"Height"},"536":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#12","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#show-more","content":"Show more"},"537":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#13","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#in-a-tool-call","content":"In a tool call"},"538":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#14","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"API"},"539":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#15","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"540":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#16","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#usage","content":"The code is one color in the theme's monospaced family: there is no syntax highlighting. For\nhighlighted, editable code, use `Editor`, which is `nsh/base`'s."},"541":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#17","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#composition","content":"Use the following composition to build a `CodeBlock`:"},"542":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#18","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#variant","content":"`variant=\"destructive\"` puts the block in the danger tone: the edge, the title and the code. Use it for errors and failed output."},"543":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#19","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#size","content":"`size=\"sm\"` has tighter padding and smaller code, for the output of a tool."},"544":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#20","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#header-and-copy","content":"`CodeBlockHeader` holds a `CodeBlockTitle`, which keeps to one line, and `CodeBlockActions`, which\nsits at the end. `CodeBlockCopyButton` is a ghost `IconButton`: a press writes `value` to the system\nclipboard and turns the icon into a check for two seconds. Its `accessibilityLabel` reads \"Copy\",\nthen \"Copied\". Put other buttons in `CodeBlockActions` beside it; a wrap toggle is the app's state,\npassed to `wrap`. There is no floating placement: the actions belong in a `CodeBlockHeader`."},"545":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#21","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#line-numbers","content":"`lineNumbers` numbers each line of a string child; `startLine` numbers from a given line, for a snippet from the middle of a file. The gutter is not selected with the code. One trailing newline does not make a line."},"546":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#22","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#lines-of-your-own","content":"`CodeBlockLine` is a line you draw yourself, with a `variant`: `highlighted` calls it out, `added` and `removed` mark a diff, each with a `+` or `−` that is not selected either. With `lineNumbers` the lines take their numbers in the order they are drawn. A block that shows a whole diff is `DiffView`."},"547":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#23","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#footer","content":"`CodeBlockFooter` is a row under the code, below a hairline: a tool's result and how long it took, or a \"Show more\" button. A string child is a note in the muted ink; other children keep the ink the app gives them."},"548":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#24","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#height","content":"Cap the height with `maxHeight` in `style` on `CodeBlockContent`; the code scrolls inside the block. `wrap` wraps long lines instead of scrolling them sideways, and suits output and errors."},"549":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#25","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#show-more","content":"Show more is the app's state: cap the content while it is collapsed and put a ghost `Button` in the footer."},"550":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#26","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#in-a-tool-call","content":"A `CodeBlock` in a card flush against its edges takes its surface off with `style`: the block's edge and corners go, a hairline stays above."},"551":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#27","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on every part but `CodeBlockTitle` (a `nsh` Text), `CodeBlockCopyButton` (an `IconButton`) and `CodeBlockContent` (a `nsh` Scroll); `style` goes over the look's. The text of the code is selectable."},"552":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#28","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"| Part        | Props                                                                                                            | Description                                                          |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CodeBlock` | `variant`: `\"default\" \\| \"destructive\"` (default `\"default\"`); `size`: `\"default\" \\| \"sm\"` (default `\"default\"`) | The surface the other parts sit in; hands its variant and size down. |","table":"table-0"},"553":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#29","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"| Part              | Props | Description                                                         |\n| ----------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CodeBlockHeader` | —     | A row above the code for a title and its actions, under a hairline. |","table":"table-0"},"554":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#30","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"| Part             | Props | Description                                            |\n| ---------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `CodeBlockTitle` | —     | A filename or a label, one line, cut with an ellipsis. |","table":"table-0"},"555":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#31","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"| Part               | Props | Description                       |\n| ------------------ | ----- | --------------------------------- |\n| `CodeBlockActions` | —     | Buttons at the end of the header. |","table":"table-0"},"556":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#32","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"| Part                  | Props                                                                                                        | Description                                                                                    |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CodeBlockCopyButton` | `value`: `string` (required); `size`: `IconButtonSize` (default `\"sm\"`); `onPress` is called before the copy | A ghost icon button that copies `value` and shows a check for two seconds (\"Copy\" → \"Copied\"). |","table":"table-0"},"557":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#33","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"| Part               | Props                                                                                                                                                     | Description                                                                                     |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CodeBlockContent` | `children`: `string \\| JSX.Element`; `lineNumbers`: `boolean` (default `false`); `startLine`: `number` (default `1`); `wrap`: `boolean` (default `false`) | The code: a string split at its newlines, or `CodeBlockLine`s. Scrolls sideways, without a bar. |","table":"table-0"},"558":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#34","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"| Part            | Props                                                                                                                                                 | Description                         |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `CodeBlockLine` | `variant`: `\"default\" \\| \"highlighted\" \\| \"added\" \\| \"removed\"` (default `\"default\"`); `lineNumber`: `number` (over the order the lines are drawn in) | One line of code you draw yourself. |","table":"table-0"},"559":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#35","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"| Part              | Props | Description                                                                                |\n| ----------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `CodeBlockFooter` | —     | A row below the code under a hairline: a result, a button. A string child is a muted note. |","table":"table-0"},"560":{"id":"/docs/components/code-block#36","page_id":"/docs/components/code-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-block#api","content":"`codeBlockLook()` is exported for a block the app draws itself: its parts as the styles they wear (`root`, `header`, `title`, `actions`, `content`, `code`, `line`, `gutter`, `marker`, `footer`, `footerText`)."},"561":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"page","content":"Collapsible","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible"},"562":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#0","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible","content":"A disclosure row that reveals a panel beneath it."},"563":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#1","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible#installation","content":"Installation"},"564":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#2","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible#usage","content":"Usage"},"565":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#3","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible#composition","content":"Composition"},"566":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#4","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible#examples","content":"Examples"},"567":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#5","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible#open-by-default","content":"Open by default"},"568":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#6","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible#closed","content":"Closed"},"569":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#7","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible#a-chevron-that-turns-over","content":"A chevron that turns over"},"570":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#8","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsible#api","content":"API"},"571":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#9","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"572":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#10","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible#composition","content":"Use the following composition to build a `Collapsible`:"},"573":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#11","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible#a-chevron-that-turns-over","content":"`chevron=\"down\"` points the chevron down and turns it over as the row opens, the way an accordion's\nturns, for a collapsible that reads as a section of one; `along` (the default) points it along the\nrow, the way a folder's does. The row takes more than one child, drawn in one line before the chevron."},"574":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#12","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible#a-chevron-that-turns-over","content":"Every trigger but the `first` draws a divider above it, inside its row, so the hover fill meets the line; `start` lines the trigger and the panel up past a leading icon. A row in the panel (`listRow`) reaches past the content, and the revealed region clips it, so give the panel room on both sides: `panel={{ start: 12, end: 12 }}`."},"575":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#13","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible#api","content":"Uses `disclosureTriggerLook`, `DisclosureChevron`, and `disclosurePanel` from accordion. Composition: `Collapsible`, `CollapsibleTrigger`, `CollapsibleContent`."},"576":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#14","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible#api","content":"| Part          | Props                                                               | Description                                       |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Collapsible` | `open`, `defaultOpen`, `onOpenChange({ open, reason })`, `children` | A disclosure row that reveals a panel beneath it. |","table":"table-0"},"577":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#15","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible#api","content":"| Part                 | Props                                                                                   | Description                                                                         |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CollapsibleTrigger` | `children`, `first`, `start`, `chevron` (`\"along\"` by default, or `\"down\"`), `disabled` | The title row; `first` drops its top divider, `start` lines it past a leading icon. |","table":"table-0"},"578":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsible#16","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsible","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsible#api","content":"| Part                 | Props                                       | Description                                      |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `CollapsibleContent` | `children`, `panel` (`start`, `end`, `gap`) | The panel beneath, in `disclosurePanel` padding. |","table":"table-0"},"579":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"page","content":"CollapsingHeader","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header"},"580":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#0","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","content":"A page's header that shrinks into a bar as the page scrolls, its picture sliding under the title."},"581":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#1","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#installation","content":"Installation"},"582":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#2","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#usage","content":"Usage"},"583":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#3","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#composition","content":"Composition"},"584":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#4","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#examples","content":"Examples"},"585":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#5","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#a-weeks-page","content":"A week's page"},"586":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#6","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#an-action-in-the-bar","content":"An action in the bar"},"587":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#7","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#a-header-with-no-picture","content":"A header with no picture"},"588":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#8","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"API"},"589":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#9","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"590":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#10","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#usage","content":"The header is the top of the page it stands in: at `expandedHeight` while the page is at its top,\ndown to `collapsedHeight` once the page has scrolled `expandedHeight - collapsedHeight`. Everything\nfollows `scroll` — the scroll view's `scrollValue` — in interpolated styles, so the collapse runs on\nthe UI thread with no JS per frame. The picture travels at half the scroll and stretches when the\npage is pulled past its top, a cover in the header's fill fades over it, the title shrinks into the\nbar and the description fades out above it. The header sticks to the top of the scroll view it is\nthe first child of, so it holds there once collapsed."},"591":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#11","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#composition","content":"Use the following composition to build a `CollapsingHeader`:"},"592":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#12","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#a-weeks-page","content":"The scene of the demo: a header over a list whose week headings stick under the bar. The bar's\nheight is `collapsingHeaderLook().heights(expandedHeight, collapsedHeight).bar` — the height the\nheader draws, whole rows in a terminal — so `stickyHeaderOffset` takes it rather than the number\npassed in."},"593":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#13","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#an-action-in-the-bar","content":"The bar is a row, so what it holds can act: the title takes the room it needs and a button comes\nafter it, in reach at every height the header has."},"594":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#14","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#a-header-with-no-picture","content":"Leave `CollapsingHeaderBackdrop` out: the header is its fill, the description and the title, and\nstill collapses. A terminal draws no picture either way."},"595":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#15","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"`CollapsingHeader` is a `nsh` View in the library's look; every\nprop of View passes through, and `style` goes over the look's. `CollapsingHeaderBackdrop`,\n`CollapsingHeaderDescription` and `CollapsingHeaderBar` take a View's too, and\n`CollapsingHeaderTitle` a `nsh` Text's; a string child of\n`CollapsingHeaderDescription` is drawn as its text."},"596":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#16","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"| Part               | Props                                                                              | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CollapsingHeader` | `scroll`: `AnimatedValue`; `expandedHeight`: `number`; `collapsedHeight`: `number` | The page's header: sticks to the top of the scroll view, `expandedHeight` tall at the page's top, `collapsedHeight` once scrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"597":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#17","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"| Part                       | Props | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| -------------------------- | ----- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CollapsingHeaderBackdrop` | —     | The picture, travelling at half the scroll and stretching on over-scroll, behind a cover that fades over it. `null` in a terminal. |","table":"table-0"},"598":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#18","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"| Part                          | Props      | Description                                          |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CollapsingHeaderDescription` | `children` | The line above the title, gone by half the collapse. |","table":"table-0"},"599":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#19","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"| Part                  | Props | Description                                                                                            |\n| --------------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `CollapsingHeaderBar` | —     | The strip at the header's bottom, `collapsedHeight` tall: a row, so it holds actions beside the title. |","table":"table-0"},"600":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#20","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"| Part                    | Props | Description                                                              |\n| ----------------------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `CollapsingHeaderTitle` | —     | The page's title, shrinking into the bar's type as the header collapses. |","table":"table-0"},"601":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#21","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"The fill is `surface(\"accent\")` — the primary colour, its ink from `surface(\"accent\").ink`, edged in the\nhairline's `brand`; the title is the display role open and the label role's size collapsed; the\ndescription is the detail's size; the bar's room either side is `density.pad` and its gap\n`density.gap`. In a terminal the heights snap to whole rows and the title does not scale. Reduced\nmotion drops the picture's travel and its stretch; the cover, the title and the description still\nfollow the scroll, since they are the collapse itself."},"602":{"id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#22","page_id":"/docs/components/collapsing-header","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/collapsing-header#api","content":"`collapsingHeaderLook()` is exported for a header an app draws itself: the heights as it draws them\n(`heights`), the parts as the styles they wear (`root`, `backdrop`, `cover`, `description`,\n`descriptionText`, `bar`, `title`, `titleClass`) and the ink the picture is drawn in (`ink`)."},"603":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"page","content":"ColorPicker","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker"},"604":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#0","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker","content":"Area, sliders, joined fields, swatches, and a popover trigger."},"605":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#1","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker#installation","content":"Installation"},"606":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#2","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker#usage","content":"Usage"},"607":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#3","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker#examples","content":"Examples"},"608":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#4","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker#panel","content":"Panel"},"609":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#5","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker#alpha","content":"Alpha"},"610":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#6","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker#swatches","content":"Swatches"},"611":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#7","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker#format","content":"Format"},"612":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#8","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"API"},"613":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#9","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"614":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#10","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#usage","content":"`ColorPopover` wraps the same panel in a field trigger. Spread `colorAreaLook()` and `colorSliderLook()` on `ColorArea` / `ColorSlider` when composing your own layout."},"615":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#11","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#panel","content":"`ColorPanel` lays out the area, the sliders, the fields and the swatches. It has to sit\ninside `nsh/base`'s `ColorPicker`: the panel's\nparts look their picker up from that root, and outside it they log\n`` `<part>` is outside a `ColorPicker`: its color goes nowhere `` and take no input."},"616":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#12","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#format","content":"`format` is one of `hex`, `rgb`, `hsl`, `hsb`, `oklch`; the fields' menu reports the reader's pick with `onFormatChange`."},"617":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#13","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"Look helpers: `colorAreaLook`, `colorSliderLook`, `formatColor`, `inkOn`. Parts: `ColorFields`, `ColorTrigger`, `ColorSwatches`, `ColorCopy`, `ColorDropper`. Behavior stays in `nsh/base` ColorPicker parts."},"618":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#14","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"| Part          | Props                                                | Description                                    |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `ColorFields` | `value`, `name`, `format`, `onFormatChange`, `alpha` | The fields of a color, with the format's menu. |","table":"table-0"},"619":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#15","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"| Part         | Props                                | Description                                                         |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ColorPanel` | every `ColorFields` prop, `swatches` | The fields with a row of swatches under them; inside `ColorPicker`. |","table":"table-0"},"620":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#16","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"| Part           | Props                                                                                    | Description                           |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `ColorPopover` | `name`, `value`, `format`, `alpha`, `style`, `onChange`, `onFormatChange`, `onChangeEnd` | The panel wrapped in a field trigger. |","table":"table-0"},"621":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#17","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"| Part           | Props                    | Description                                         |\n| -------------- | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ColorTrigger` | `open`, `value`, `style` | The field that shows the color and opens the panel. |","table":"table-0"},"622":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#18","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"| Part            | Props    | Description                              |\n| --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `ColorSwatches` | `colors` | The row of swatches, one of them chosen. |","table":"table-0"},"623":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#19","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"| Part        | Props          | Description                                   |\n| ----------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `ColorCopy` | `name`, `text` | Copies the value; a check shows for a moment. |","table":"table-0"},"624":{"id":"/docs/components/color-picker#20","page_id":"/docs/components/color-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/color-picker#api","content":"| Part           | Props  | Description                                                |\n| -------------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ColorDropper` | `name` | The system eyedropper, hidden where the platform has none. |","table":"table-0"},"625":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"page","content":"Combobox","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox"},"626":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#0","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox","content":"A searchable field with a list of choices and chips for the values chosen, on the shared listbox look."},"627":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#1","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#installation","content":"Installation"},"628":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#2","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#usage","content":"Usage"},"629":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#3","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#composition","content":"Composition"},"630":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#4","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#examples","content":"Examples"},"631":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#5","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#disabled-and-clearable","content":"Disabled and clearable"},"632":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#6","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#one-value","content":"One value"},"633":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#7","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#several-values","content":"Several values"},"634":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#8","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#chips-in-the-field","content":"Chips in the field"},"635":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#9","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#groups-and-an-empty-list","content":"Groups and an empty list"},"636":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#10","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#a-trigger-of-your-own","content":"A trigger of your own"},"637":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#11","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"API"},"638":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#12","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"639":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#13","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#usage","content":"The examples draw icons with `Icon` from `lib/ui/icons`; see Icons for adding it and picking a size and color."},"640":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#14","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#usage","content":"Without `multiple`, `value` is the chosen item or `null` (`string | null`). With `multiple`, it is the chosen items (`string[]`)."},"641":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#15","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#composition","content":"Use the following composition to build a `Combobox`:"},"642":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#16","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#one-value","content":"Leave `multiple` out. A choice replaces the last one and closes the list. `onChange` receives `{ value: string | null }`."},"643":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#17","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#one-value","content":"The trigger opens and closes the list. The field's input takes typing, and typing opens the list\nfiltered as you type (`nsh/base` also toggles on the input's press — `references/nsh/crates/nsh-base/src/combobox.rs`,\nits `on_press` — but a click on macOS lands in the field editor for the caret,\n`references/nsh/crates/nsh-platform-macos/src/text_input.rs`, so with a pointer the arrow is the way\nin). Clicking the field puts the caret there and does not open the list; tabbing into it does not\neither."},"644":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#18","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#several-values","content":"`multiple` toggles an item and keeps the list open; the field shows the chosen titles."},"645":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#19","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#chips-in-the-field","content":"`ComboboxChips` draws the chosen values as chips at the start of the field — where NSH puts a\nmultiple combobox's `prefix` — so the input keeps the query and the field grows down as the chips\nwrap. A chip's label is its item's title, and its remove button drops that value."},"646":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#20","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#chips-in-the-field","content":"A chip can take a mark at its start (`lead`) or keep its value against a stray press\n(`showRemove={false}`); a function child draws each value's chip instead of the default one:"},"647":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#21","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#chips-in-the-field","content":"The chips are that `prefix`, not a field of their own: typing beside them still filters through the\ncombobox's input, and a text field of its own beside the chips is a second control."},"648":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#22","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#chips-in-the-field","content":"`ComboboxChip` and `ComboboxChips` render only inside `<Combobox>` — as `ComboboxChips` (the field's\nprefix) or anywhere else under that root, including as a sibling of `ComboboxContent`. Outside the\nroot they throw. A chip drawn somewhere else, a summary beside the field, is the app's own: read\n`value` and update it from the chip's press."},"649":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#23","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#a-trigger-of-your-own","content":"A string child is a `Button`; anything else is drawn as given. `testID` reaches the\nbutton or the default toggle, and `accessibilityLabel` names it (the default toggle is a\nchevron with no text of its own)."},"650":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#24","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"The root owns the open flag and the chosen values; `ComboboxContent` mounts `nsh/base` Combobox and every base prop passes through except those. The combobox look, `listboxProps` and `OptionRow` fill the field, the popup and the rows by default."},"651":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#25","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part       | Props                                                                                                                                                                                                               | Description                                                                                                                            |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Combobox` | `value` / `defaultValue` (`string \\| null`, or `string[]` with `multiple`), `multiple`, `open` / `defaultOpen`, `disabled`, `cleanable`, `placeholder`, `onChange`, `onOpenChange`, `onOpen`, `onClose`, `onCancel` | The root: one value, or several when `multiple` is set. `onChange` follows that: `{ value: string \\| null }` or `{ value: string[] }`. |","table":"table-0"},"652":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#26","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part              | Props                                                                      | Description                                                     |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ComboboxTrigger` | `children`, `variant`, `disabled`, `testID`, `accessibilityLabel`, `style` | The disclosure at the field's end (a `ComboToggle` by default). |","table":"table-0"},"653":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#27","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part              | Props                                                                | Description                                                           |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ComboboxContent` | `items` (instead of `ComboboxItem` children), `minWidth`, `children` | The field and the list anchored to it; it mounts `nsh/base` Combobox. |","table":"table-0"},"654":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#28","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part           | Props                                                            | Description             |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `ComboboxItem` | `value`, `disabled`, `group`, `children` (a string is its title) | One choice in the list. |","table":"table-0"},"655":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#29","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part            | Props                                                                                   | Description                                                       |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ComboboxChips` | `children`: a `(value) => JSX.Element` that draws each one, a `ComboboxChip` by default | The chosen values as chips at the field's start (NSH's `prefix`). |","table":"table-0"},"656":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#30","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part           | Props                                                                                                       | Description                                          |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ComboboxChip` | `value`, `children` (its text, the item's title by default), `lead`, `showRemove` (default `true`), `style` | One value's chip. It has to sit inside `<Combobox>`. |","table":"table-0"},"657":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#31","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part            | Props      | Description            |\n| --------------- | ---------- | ---------------------- |\n| `ComboboxGroup` | `children` | A section of the list. |","table":"table-0"},"658":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#32","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part            | Props                 | Description       |\n| --------------- | --------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `ComboboxLabel` | `children` (a string) | A section's name. |","table":"table-0"},"659":{"id":"/docs/components/combobox#33","page_id":"/docs/components/combobox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/combobox#api","content":"| Part            | Props                    | Description                                          |\n| --------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ComboboxEmpty` | `children` (the message) | What the list shows while the query matches nothing. |","table":"table-0"},"660":{"id":"/docs/components/command","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"page","content":"Command","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command"},"661":{"id":"/docs/components/command#0","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command","content":"A search palette with sectioned, virtualized rows."},"662":{"id":"/docs/components/command#1","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command#installation","content":"Installation"},"663":{"id":"/docs/components/command#2","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command#usage","content":"Usage"},"664":{"id":"/docs/components/command#3","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command#examples","content":"Examples"},"665":{"id":"/docs/components/command#4","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command#groups","content":"Groups"},"666":{"id":"/docs/components/command#5","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command#shortcut-and-check","content":"Shortcut and check"},"667":{"id":"/docs/components/command#6","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command#search","content":"Search"},"668":{"id":"/docs/components/command#7","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command#a-long-list","content":"A long list"},"669":{"id":"/docs/components/command#8","page_id":"/docs/components/command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/command#api","content":"API"},"670":{"id":"/docs/components/command#9","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"671":{"id":"/docs/components/command#10","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#groups","content":"Rows with the same `group` gather under its heading, in the order given; `disabled` dims a row."},"672":{"id":"/docs/components/command#11","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#shortcut-and-check","content":"`shortcut` is drawn with a pointer in `kbd`'s key cap, the library's one (`add command` brings it); `checked` marks the row in effect."},"673":{"id":"/docs/components/command#12","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#search","content":"The field filters the rows as you type. The shell sets the search bar's row and the field's text\nand placeholder color inline, over `commandClasses`, so an icon in `searchPrefix` stays beside the\nfield and the placeholder stays the muted foreground — including when `searchable` turns the bar on\nafter the palette has mounted. A caller's `searchBarStyle` and `searchStyle` win over those."},"674":{"id":"/docs/components/command#13","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#a-long-list","content":"The rows are made as they come into view, so five thousand files cost what five do: `listClass`\ngives the list its height and the rest scrolls. `keywords` let the query find a file by its\nextension as well as by its name (`png` finds every image), `renderItem` draws the extension's\nicon, and the ref's `matchedCount()` is what the query left — the count under the palette reads\nit, never the app's guess at the filter."},"675":{"id":"/docs/components/command#14","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#api","content":"Uses `commandClasses`, `CommandRow`, `CommandHeading`, and `CommandEmpty` by default. Every prop of `nsh/base` Command passes through."},"676":{"id":"/docs/components/command#15","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#api","content":"| Part      | Props | Description                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------- | ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `Command` | —     | A command palette: a search field over virtualized, natively filtered rows, however many there are. `searchBarStyle` and `searchStyle` still pass through, over the shell's row and placeholder color. |","table":"table-0"},"677":{"id":"/docs/components/command#16","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#api","content":"| Part         | Props                             | Description                                                                                                        |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `CommandRow` | `entry`, `icon`, `detail`, `note` | A row's content: the icon, the label, a `note` at the end, the shortcut's keys and a check for the item in effect. |","table":"table-0"},"678":{"id":"/docs/components/command#17","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#api","content":"| Part             | Props   | Description                                             |\n| ---------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CommandHeading` | `group` | A section's heading: small capitals in the faint color. |","table":"table-0"},"679":{"id":"/docs/components/command#18","page_id":"/docs/components/command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/command#api","content":"| Part           | Props   | Description                                   |\n| -------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `CommandEmpty` | `label` | What the palette shows while nothing matches. |","table":"table-0"},"680":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"page","content":"Context Menu","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu"},"681":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#0","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu","content":"A menu at the pointer, on the shared menu look."},"682":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#1","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#installation","content":"Installation"},"683":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#2","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#usage","content":"Usage"},"684":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#3","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#composition","content":"Composition"},"685":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#4","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#examples","content":"Examples"},"686":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#5","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#a-surface","content":"A surface"},"687":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#6","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#separator-and-a-destructive-item","content":"Separator and a destructive item"},"688":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#7","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#keep-it-open","content":"Keep it open"},"689":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#8","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#a-checkable-row-and-its-neighbours","content":"A checkable row and its neighbours"},"690":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#9","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#open-change","content":"Open change"},"691":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#10","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-menu#api","content":"API"},"692":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#11","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"693":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#12","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#composition","content":"Use the following composition to build a `ContextMenu`:"},"694":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#13","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#a-surface","content":"Any view can be the trigger; the menu opens at the pointer on a secondary click or a long press."},"695":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#14","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#keep-it-open","content":"`closeOnSelect={false}` leaves the menu up for a toggle inside it."},"696":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#15","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#a-checkable-row-and-its-neighbours","content":"A checkable row keeps its mark's room whether it is checked or not, so its label stays put as it\nis toggled. `inset` gives the plain rows of the same menu that room too, and their labels line up\nwith it. `ContextMenuLabel` and `ContextMenuSubTrigger` take it as well."},"697":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#16","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#api","content":"Row and popup looks come from Menu. Items, separators, labels and submenus are re-exported as `ContextMenu*` parts. There is no radio-group part: a `ContextMenuGroup` holds the rows, and each `ContextMenuRadioItem` carries its own `checked`."},"698":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#17","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#api","content":"| Part          | Props                                                                                                | Description                     |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `ContextMenu` | `open`, `defaultOpen`, `disabled`, `onOpenChange({ open, reason })`, `onOpen`, `onClose`, `onCancel` | Open state and the trigger slot |","table":"table-0"},"699":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#18","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#api","content":"| Part                 | Props               | Description                                                                            |\n| -------------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ContextMenuTrigger` | `children`, `style` | Secondary click or long press; wraps its children, in a `View` when it takes a `style` |","table":"table-0"},"700":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#19","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#api","content":"| Part                 | Props                                                                                                                                                    | Description        |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `ContextMenuContent` | every `nsh/base` ContextMenu prop but open state, `disabled`, `trigger` and the lifecycle callbacks; `offset` (default 4), `popupStyle`, `backdropStyle` | The popup or sheet |","table":"table-0"},"701":{"id":"/docs/components/context-menu#20","page_id":"/docs/components/context-menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-menu#api","content":"| Part                | Props                    | Description                           |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `ContextMenuItem` … | as the Menu counterparts | Rows, labels, separators and submenus |","table":"table-0"},"702":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"page","content":"DataTable","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table"},"703":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#0","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table","content":"A striped table with sortable, resizable columns."},"704":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#1","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#installation","content":"Installation"},"705":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#2","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#usage","content":"Usage"},"706":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#3","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#examples","content":"Examples"},"707":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#4","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#columns","content":"Columns"},"708":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#5","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#stripes","content":"Stripes"},"709":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#6","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#a-fixed-body","content":"A fixed body"},"710":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#7","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#fit-padding","content":"Fit padding"},"711":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#8","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#fixed-columns","content":"Fixed columns"},"712":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#9","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#selecting","content":"Selecting"},"713":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#10","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/data-table#api","content":"API"},"714":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#11","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"715":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#12","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#columns","content":"`width`, `align` and `sortable` are per column."},"716":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#13","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#a-fixed-body","content":"The table fills and scrolls in the box it is given."},"717":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#14","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#fit-padding","content":"A column fitted to its content takes `fitPadding` for the room the drawing adds beside the text: a\ncolumn of this look sets **16** — 8 points before a cell's text, 4 after it, and the 4-point gap\nbefore a header's sort button."},"718":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#15","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#fixed-columns","content":"`fixed: true` pins a column at the leading edge (`\"left\"` and `\"right\"` say which edge) while the\nrest scroll horizontally under it. Fixed columns lead the row, take their width from `width`\n(content cannot set it) and keep their place in the header too; the seam between a pinned column\nand the scrolling body is `fixedEdge` in `dataTableClasses`. Give the table more columns than fit\nthe box to see it work."},"719":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#16","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#selecting","content":"Rows select by default; `columnSelectable` lets titles select columns and `cellSelectable` lets\ncells select. `onSelectionChange` reports the `{ row, column }` selection (both zero-based), and\n`selection` sets it back — a controlled selection, so what stays selected is the app's call. A\nselection of a kind that does not select is cleared."},"720":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#17","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#selecting","content":"A selection of several is the app's too: set `selectOnModifierPress={false}`, keep your own range or\nset in `onRowPress` / `onColumnPress` (each reports Shift, Control, Option and the clicks), and paint\nit with `rowClasses`, `cellClasses` or the columns' `headerClass` / `cellClass`."},"721":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#18","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#api","content":"| Part        | Props                                                              | Description                             |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------- |\n| `DataTable` | every `nsh/base` DataTable prop; `classes` over `dataTableClasses` | A striped table, sortable and resizable |","table":"table-0"},"722":{"id":"/docs/components/data-table#19","page_id":"/docs/components/data-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/data-table#api","content":"Uses `dataTableClasses`. Every prop of `nsh/base` DataTable passes through."},"723":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","type":"page","content":"Date Picker","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/date-picker"},"724":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#0","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker","content":"A calendar in a popup from a field trigger, on the shared listbox look."},"725":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#1","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/date-picker#installation","content":"Installation"},"726":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#2","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/date-picker#usage","content":"Usage"},"727":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#3","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","type":"heading","tags":