r#a-range","content":"`range` on the content; the trigger shows both ends. After the first pick the band previews the\nrange to the day under the pointer or the keyboard, as the calendar's does."},"738":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#14","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#clearable-and-a-placeholder","content":"Without a value the trigger shows `placeholder` (default \"Pick a date\") muted."},"739":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#15","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#api","content":"| Part         | Props                                                                                                                                                 | Description              |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `DatePicker` | `value` / `defaultValue`, `open` / `defaultOpen`, `disabled`, `cleanable`, `placeholder`, `onChange`, `onOpenChange`, `onOpen`, `onClose`, `onCancel` | Open state and the value |","table":"table-0"},"740":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#16","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#api","content":"| Part                | Props                                                                                                       | Description                                                |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `DatePickerTrigger` | `title` (default the value), `placeholder`, `invalid`, `clearable`, `style`, `testID`, `accessibilityLabel` | A `DateTrigger`, the pressed field that opens the calendar |","table":"table-0"},"741":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#17","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#api","content":"| Part                | Props                                                                      | Description               |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `DatePickerContent` | `range`, `timePrecision`, `presets`, `numberOfMonths`, `firstDayOfWeek`, … | The calendar in the popup |","table":"table-0"},"742":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker#18","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#api","content":"`testID` finds the trigger in UI tests, and `accessibilityLabel` names it when the\ncontent does not name the field. The root owns the open flag and the value;\n`DatePickerContent` mounts `nsh/base` DatePicker\nand every base prop passes through except those. The date picker's look fills the popup, the scrim, the calendar and the time's row by default."},"743":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"page","content":"Dialog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog"},"744":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#0","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog","content":"A card dialog with a trigger, content, title, description, footer and close."},"745":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#1","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#installation","content":"Installation"},"746":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#2","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#usage","content":"Usage"},"747":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#3","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#composition","content":"Composition"},"748":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#4","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#examples","content":"Examples"},"749":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#5","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#width","content":"Width"},"750":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#6","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#motion","content":"Motion"},"751":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#7","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#presentation","content":"Presentation"},"752":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#8","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#scrolling","content":"Scrolling"},"753":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#9","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#a-page-of-its-own","content":"A page of its own"},"754":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#10","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#closing","content":"Closing"},"755":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#11","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#card-and-backdrop","content":"Card and backdrop"},"756":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#12","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"757":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#13","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"API"},"758":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#14","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#installation","content":"As a TSX module, added once per app — nothing is copied into it:"},"759":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#15","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#composition","content":"Use the following composition to build a `Dialog`:"},"760":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#16","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#width","content":"The card is 360 points with a pointer and 320 on a touch screen; `width` sets another, never past 90% of the window."},"761":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#17","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#motion","content":"`animation` is `fade` (the card's default), `slide`, or `none`."},"762":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#18","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#presentation","content":"`presentation` hands the dialog to the system: `fullScreen` comes up over the window, `pageSheet` and `formSheet` come up as the system's sheet, with what is behind them still in sight (iOS). The system draws the card there — its edge, its radius, its shadow, its place and its height — so the content wears no card, and the app's `style` starts from a page (`dialogPage`) instead. Desktops and the web ignore `presentation`: there the card stands."},"763":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#19","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#scrolling","content":"The card is never taller than the window holds inside the safe areas, 24 points clear of either edge, and its body scrolls under that cap. `DialogFooter` is drawn under the scrolling body, so the actions stay put; `DialogTitle` and `DialogDescription` are in the body and scroll with it (put them in their own block if the title has to stay)."},"764":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#20","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#scrolling","content":"`scroll={false}` draws the children as given, with no scroll of the shell's: for a body that takes gestures of its own."},"765":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#21","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#a-page-of-its-own","content":"A dialog the app fills the window with — a lightbox, an editor — passes `dialogPage()` as `style`: it takes the card's edge, radius, shadow, padding, width and height cap off and fills what the dialog gives it."},"766":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#22","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#closing","content":"Escape, a backdrop press and a downward swipe close the dialog; turn any of them off on the content."},"767":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#23","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#card-and-backdrop","content":"`style` goes over the card's chrome, `backdropStyle` over the scrim."},"768":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#24","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#controlled","content":"`open` owns the state; `onOpenChange` reports the next one and why."},"769":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#25","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"`Dialog` owns the open state. `DialogContent` mounts `nsh/base` Dialog; every base prop passes through it, and base owns the backdrop, the popup host and Escape, back and swipe."},"770":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#26","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"| Part     | Props                                                                                    | Description |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `Dialog` | `open`, `defaultOpen`, `onOpenChange({ open, reason })`, `onOpen`, `onClose`, `onCancel` | Open state  |","table":"table-0"},"771":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#27","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"| Part            | Props                                      | Description           |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------ | --------------------- |\n| `DialogTrigger` | `children`, `variant`, `disabled`, `style` | What opens the dialog |","table":"table-0"},"772":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#28","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"| Part            | Props                                                                                                                                                                 | Description |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `DialogContent` | `width`, `scroll`, every `nsh/base` Dialog prop (`presentation`); `style` over the card (or `dialogPage` when the system presents it), `backdropStyle` over the scrim | The card    |","table":"table-0"},"773":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#29","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"| Part          | Props                                    | Description      |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `DialogTitle` | `children`; a string takes `dialogTitle` | The card's title |","table":"table-0"},"774":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#30","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"| Part                | Props                                   | Description                    |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `DialogDescription` | `children`; a string takes `dialogText` | The muted line under the title |","table":"table-0"},"775":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#31","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"| Part           | Props               | Description                                                    |\n| -------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `DialogFooter` | `children`, `style` | The row of actions at the card's end, under the scrolling body |","table":"table-0"},"776":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#32","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"| Part          | Props                                               | Description            |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `DialogClose` | As `DialogTrigger`, plus `onPress` before it closes | What closes the dialog |","table":"table-0"},"777":{"id":"/docs/components/dialog#33","page_id":"/docs/components/dialog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/dialog#api","content":"A string child of `DialogTrigger` or `DialogClose` is a `Button`; `variant` picks its look (`secondary` by default). Anything else is drawn as given."},"778":{"id":"/docs/components/diff-view","page_id":"/docs/components/diff-view","type":"page","content":"DiffView","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/diff-view"},"779":{"id":"/docs/components/diff-view#0","page_id":"/docs/components/diff-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/diff-view","content":"Up and down tints for additions and deletions, with hunk actions."},"780":{"id":"/docs/components/diff-view#1","page_id":"/docs/components/diff-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/diff-view#installation","content":"Installation"},"781":{"id":"/docs/components/diff-view#2","page_id":"/docs/components/diff-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"u