f the app's own takes `desktop={{ windowDrag: true }}` to drag the window, and pads by\n`titleBar().left` and `titleBar().right` so its content clears the system's buttons."],[1628,"A bar over the document, every control reading the caret: the block it stands in, the marks it\ncarries, the list around it. The session re-reads on each `revision`, so `isActive` and `can` are\ncurrent when the bar draws; a control whose command cannot run where the caret stands is `disabled`\n(`can`), and a press runs the command and puts the caret back with `focus()` — or the document loses\nit to the button. `command` builds the Tiptap commands by name; the list indents are\n`sinkListItem` and `liftListItem` over `listItem`."],[2147,"A bar without `ToolbarOverflow` behaves identically to a static bar. In a bar with `ToolbarOverflow`\non a horizontal non-terminal surface, unmeasured items stay visible rather than blocking folding.\nBecause `nsh/base`'s `Button`, `Toggle` and `Link` do not forward `onFocus`/`onBlur`, `Toolbar` does\nnot expose `onFocusIn`/`onFocusOut`, and `nsh/base`'s roving focus marks non-stop items\n`focusable={false}` (`roving.rs`), focus cannot automatically move to `\"⋯\"` when a focused tool\nfolds while an earlier tool remains visible."],[1811,"A block of content"],[2019,"A block of your own"],[900,"A block that says one thing"],[1728,"A bottom sheet can rest at heights instead of fitting its content: `detents` names them (`\"medium\"`\nis half the screen, `\"large\"` its room), and a drag or a press on the grabber moves between them. Pass\n`detent` and `onDetentChange` to own which one it rests at, and leave `closeOnSwipe` on to let a\ndownward swipe below the smallest close it."],[1726,"A bottom sheet has a grabber at its top: `nsh/base`'s own handle, which screen readers adjust to\nchange the detent and which moves to the next larger one when pressed. It is the handle itself,\nnot a picture of one, so a sheet never shows two. `grabber`\noff shows it; `grabberAccessibilityLabel` names it (\"Sheet\" by default)."],[194,"A box as wide as its column and as tall as its ratio says."],[15,"A built-in theme distills a design system's colors, radii, surfaces, and motion. It does not clone that system's widgets one to one."],[383,"A button, an icon button, and a round button."],[724,"A calendar in a popup from a field trigger, on the shared listbox look."],[2187,"A call goes `pending` (dimmed), `running`, then done (no status), and opens onto what it did. The result is a `CodeBlock`: a search, a weather lookup and a code run are the same `Trace` with a different body — a list of `Item`s, a card, a `CodeBlock` — not a card of their own. Disable the trigger until there is something to show."],[1482,"A candle is a `Bar` from the open to the close and a `Rule` from the low to the high, both colored\nby a `\"dir\"` category. The volume is a second `Plot` under the price one, sharing its band scale so\nthe bars line up, with its own right axis:"],[1108,"A cap is a view, not a span of a paragraph: in running text the sentence is a row of `Text` and\n`KbdGroup`, wrapping together."],[744,"A card dialog with a trigger, content, title, description, footer and close."],[466,"A card takes the width its style gives it; `flexGrow` with `flexBasis` puts two across a window\nand one across a phone."],[893,"A centered block that says there is nothing here yet, and what to do about it."],[1263,"A chat"],[689,"A checkable row and its neighbours"],[696,"A checkable row keeps its mark's room whether it is checked or not, so its label stays put as it\nis toggled. `inset` gives the plain rows of the same menu that room too, and their labels line up\nwith it. `ContextMenuLabel` and `ContextMenuSubTrigger` take it as well."],[569,"A chevron that turns over"],[646,"A chip can take a mark at its start (`lead`) or keep its value against a stray press\n(`showRemove={false}`); a function child draws each value's chip instead of the default one:"],[201,"A color block"],[363,"A column"],[717,"A column fitted to its content takes `fitPadding` for the room the drawing adds beside the text: a\ncolumn of this look sets **16** — 8 points before a cell's text, 4 after it, and the 4-point gap\nbefore a header's sort button."],[882,"A composer keeps the panel behind a `Popover` on the field's leading addon. Choosing closes the\npanel and puts the emoji at the end of the draft; `base` (the emoji without its skin tone) is what\nleads the recents, so the tab that holds it opens first the next time."],[118,"A confirmation of the platform's own."],[2398,"A control's own geometry and face live in the theme too, so switching themes changes its shape, not only its colours. `control(name)` resolves one for the active theme and the device's input tier:"],[1279,"A conversation starts with an empty frame: keep the greeting and its suggestions inside the\n`MessageScroller` until the first turn arrives, so the frame holds its height and the composer under\nit never jumps. `MessageScrollerProvider` shares the scroller with that composer, and the send\nbutton is a `RoundButton` beside an `Input`."],[1253,"A conversation that keeps up with itself: new turns follow the newest message while you are at the end, and wait when you are not."],[2060,"A desktop window with `titleBar: { style: \"hidden\" }` keeps the system's window buttons and leaves\nthe rest of the bar to the app: `TitleBar` builds on `nsh/base`'s `TitleBar` to draw the bar, drag\nthe window, double click to zoom or maximize, and keep its children clear of the system buttons\nautomatically across split panes and full-screen transitions."],[1190,"A destructive item"],[1538,"A determinate or indeterminate progress bar."],[765,"A dialog the app fills the window with — a lightbox, an editor — passes `dialogPage()` as `style`: it takes the card's edge, radius, shadow, padding, width and height cap off and fills what the dialog gives it."],[1011,"A disabled group disables what it holds and