 missing entries into `theme.json` while keeping your values."],[2264,"Add shadcn-nsh to an existing NSH app."],[999,"Addons over and under the control"],[2236,"After an update"],[123,"Against `Dialog`"],[826,"Against `Sheet`"],[159,"Alert"],[117,"Alert Dialog"],[327,"Alignment"],[1312,"Alignment"],[1923,"Alone"],[609,"Alpha"],[1486,"Also export `Legend` for a colored square and label beside a chart."],[1611,"Also export `resizableHandleLook` and `handleThumb` for a handle the app lays out itself."],[1079,"An `Item` is layout only: it draws a row and takes no presses, so the container decides what a row\ndoes. For a row that is a control — hover fill, keyboard focus, disabled — use the same content on\n`listRow` instead, or wrap it in a view with `onPress` and `role=\"button\"`. `ItemGroup` is\n`role=\"list\"`, but NSH has no `listitem` role, so an `Item` is a plain view and a reader moves\nthrough its text element by element: when the rows can be pressed, mark the pressable view\n`role=\"button\"` and give it an `accessibilityLabel` that says the whole row (or use `listRow`,\nwhich does)."],[586,"An action in the bar"],[1774,"An action is always there: hover alone is something a touch screen has no way to do."],[1749,"An action, a badge"],[2085,"An action's `onClick` runs when it is pressed, and `onDismiss` hears that action's label — or `null` when the toast leaves any other way."],[996,"An addon before and after the input"],[2174,"An agent's steps, one line each — reasoning, a tool call, a source, a failed step — where a line can open onto what it did."],[2247,"An app that only needs different colors can edit the copied `theme.json`. A later `add` merges keys the file lacks and keeps values you changed, unless you pass `--overwrite`. Surfaces, controls, metrics, and motion are not in `theme.json`. Those stay on the spec, in `themes/<id>.ts` after a copy, or in the module `nshm` resolves. Theme specification lists the roles. Architecture is the three layers."],[145,"An app that wants the choice before it draws anything else — `await`, then act — shows the same box\nwith `nsh/base`'s own `AlertDialog.show`, which resolves with `{ action, value }`. That is the app's call.\nThe parts above declare a box under a root of the page's, for an alert that is part of what the page\ndraws; the library has no imperative `show` of its own: a web alert is\nalways the app's own drawing, and a second way in would be two APIs for one box."],[1996,"An app whose window is the terminal"],[2280,"An app with `nsh.json` (from `nsh init`) is ready:"],[2408,"An app's `nsh.json` sets the look in two places, and the two do not merge:"],[1739,"An app's navigation column beside its page — folded to a strip of icons, or sliding in as a sheet on a phone."],[845,"An editor on the field's well, with line numbers, diagnostics and a find bar."],[941,"An error is announced where the platform does it by itself. `FieldError` is a view with\n`role=\"alert\"` (macOS and the web read it when it appears) and TalkBack's live region\n(`accessibilityLiveRegion: \"assertive\"` on Android). iOS has no live region: `UIAccessibility`'s\nannouncement is the app's call, and NSH does not expose it — put the message in the control's\n`accessibilityHint` there as well if it must be heard the moment it appears. Mark the control\ninvalid, not just the field: pass `invalid` to the control (an `Input`, a `Select`'s trigger),\nbecause `role=\"alert\"` tells a reader that something is wrong, not which field."],[2028,"An extension claims a Markdown shape for the app. A `language` claims a fence; `renderCustom`\nreceives the node, with `node.text` the fence's source, and returns the view to draw in its place.\nHere a `chart` fence lists `label value` lines and becomes bars in the theme's brand color."],[1630,"An extension's node view: `addNodeView` returns the app's own component, and the editor draws\nevery node of that type with it — the component runs when a node appears, and its props change in\nplace when the node's attributes or its selection do. `RichNodeViewProps` carries `node` (its\n`attrs`), `selected` (it takes presses, so the caret steps over an atom as one character and\nBackspace deletes it) and the session's own `updateAttributes` / `deleteNode` for a node that edits\nitself. Typing never runs the component."],[177,"An icon and a title are a notice of one line."],[2313,"An icon value from `lucide` has the same shape (`[tag, attrs][]`) and assigns to `IconNode`. Pass one anywhere a component takes an icon."],[1093,"An icon's tile is `controlSize.control + 12` square and an image's frame `controlSize.row - 8`,\nboth of the theme's control corners, so both grow on a touch screen. `itemLook()` is exported for a\nrow the app draws itself: the same look without the parts. `muted`'s fill is the theme's `muted`\ntoken (`token(\"muted\")`); `default` and `outline` draw what they always did."],[978,"An image viewer"],[2030,"An inline extension replaces each match of its `pattern` with the node the app draws. Keep the\nchip's `verticalAlign` at `middle` and its height under the line height, so the paragraph's lines\nkeep their spacing; `styles.root.lineHeight` gives the chip the room it needs."],[2125,"An inset track of tools, with groups and hairline separators."],[1915,"An on / off switch whose knob springs across a sunk track."],[824,"Another edge"],[393,"Any content"],[694,"Any view can be the trigger; the menu opens at the pointer on a secondary click or a long press."],[1333,"Anything else in `MessageFooter` is drawn as given: a row of `IconButton`s, a retry, an error."],[104,"API"],[131,"API"],[172,"API"],[202,"API"],[223,"API"],[259,"API"],[280,"API"],[299,"API"],[333,"API"],[367,"API"],[398,"API"],[445,"API"],[462,"API"],[489,"API"],[515,"API"],[538,"API"],[570,"API"],[588,"API"],[612,"API"],[637,"API"],[669,"API"],[691,"API"],[713,"API"],[734,"API"],[757,"API"],[788,"API"],[805,"API"],[827,"API"],[856,"API"],[880,"API"],[902,"API"],