s the `nsh` element it is drawn with. Every view prop passes through; `style` goes over\nthe part's own."],[2421,"Edit the spec; every component follows. Change a brand colour in `tokens.light` and `tokens.dark`, a radius in `tokens.radius`, a shadow part in `elevation`, a gradient, a surface or a control in the theme's own `index.ts` — then `bun run theme:build` re-exports `theme.json`, `DESIGN.md` and the two `.tokens.json` files. Keep the keys: components and surfaces refer to them by name. A value that follows the device is stated twice, `pointer` and `touch`, with the same keys."],[844,"Editor"],[872,"Emoji picker"],[892,"Empty"],[2221,"Enhanced"],[929,"Errors"],[766,"Escape, a backdrop press and a downward swipe close the dialog; turn any of them off on the content."],[2415,"Every `theme.json` writes `font-sans` and `font-mono`. Built-in themes leave `tokens.font` unset, so those keys are `system-ui` and `monospace` — the system's own faces — and one type scale (sizes and line heights) serves them all, so switching themes never reflows text. Each theme states its own weight and letter spacing per role. `font.sans` and `font.mono` read the two keys; the `font-sans` and `font-mono` classes read the same CSS variables. The user's system font size scales every size."],[2289,"Every command takes `-c, --cwd <dir>` (default: the current directory). `init`, `add`, `list`, `view` and `diff` also take `--registry <url>`, a template with `{name}` in it. CLI has every flag and default."],[2530,"Every demo on this site can be drawn in any of these palettes: pick one with the **Demo theme**\nswitch in the nav, and the previews load again in it. The panel above is the showcase — buttons, a\ncard with a field, badges, switches, a slider and a progress bar, with the card, inset and press surfaces\nthe palette brings. The list is `apps/website/demos/palettes.ts`. Each palette has its own page,\nwith the same sections: how to install it, every token it sets, and every surface it draws. Those\npages read each theme's own spec. The contract is\n`docs/theme.md`."],[1218,"Every part that draws a view takes `nsh`'s view props and spreads them on it after its own look, so an app's `testID`, `accessibilityLabel`, `onLongPress` or `class` reaches the row it passes them to; `style` goes over the look's, and the states an app passes (`hoverStyle`, `focusStyle`, `activeStyle`, `disabledStyle`) are merged after the look's own. `Menu` and `MenuSub` draw no view of their own (they own the open state and the trigger slot), so they take none: an app gives those props to the trigger or the content."],[1534,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Button passes through (`onPress`, `disabled`, `selected`, `role`, `hitSlop`, `accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityHint`, …). `style`, `hoverStyle`, `activeStyle` and `focusVisibleStyle` go over the look's. `scale` is the sink of a press."],[419,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Button passes through. `style`, `hoverStyle`, `activeStyle`, `focusVisibleStyle` and `disabledStyle` go over the look's."],[519,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Checkbox passes through. `indicatorClass` and `indicatorStyle` go over the look's. The row is the `group` the box sinks with while pressed."],[797,"Every prop of `nsh/base` DiffView passes through."],[858,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Editor passes through: the text (`value` / `defaultValue`, `onChange`), the language and its highlighting, folding, soft wrap, search, the editing keys and the diagnostics. The shell adds the look of the editor's parts and the field's well."],[1054,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Input passes through. `class`, `style` and `disabledStyle` go over the look's. Focus and hover edges are classes on the look."],[1154,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Link passes through."],[1236,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Menu passes through on `MenubarContent`\nexcept the trigger, the open state and the lifecycle callbacks, which the root owns. `popupStyle`,\n`backdropStyle` and `popupStartingStyle` go over `menuPopup`'s. Defaults: `placement` `\"bottom\"`,\n`align` `\"start\"`, `offset` `8` — a menu under the trigger it belongs to, whatever the bar's width."],[1430,"Every prop of `nsh/base` NumberInput passes through. `class`, `inputStyle` and the step props go over the look's."],[1443,"Every prop of `nsh/base` OtpInput passes through. Cell and caret props go over the look's."],[1576,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Radio and `RadioGroup` passes through. Style props go over the look's. The row is the `group` the ring sinks with while pressed. `RadioGroupItem` is an alias of `Radio`."],[843,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Sheet passes through on `DrawerContent`\nexcept open state and the lifecycle callbacks, which the root owns. `popupStyle` and `backdropStyle`\ngo over the look's. Defaults: `side` `\"bottom\"`, `closeOnSwipe` `true`."],[1732,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Sheet passes through on `SheetContent`. `popupStyle` and `backdropStyle` go over the look's."],[1936,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Switch passes through. `trackClass`, `trackStyle` and `thumbStyle` go over the look's."],[1989,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Tabs / `Tab` passes through on the list and triggers."],[2008,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Terminal passes through, and so does\nits ref (`TerminalRef`): `write`, `reset`, `text`, `focus`. `class`, `style`, `cursorClass` and\n`cursorStyle` go over the look's, so an app gives the cursor its shape (`w-0.5`) and moves the\npadding where it needs another."],[2045,"Every prop of `nsh/base` TimeField passes through; `class`, `segmentClass`, `separatorStyle` and `renderSegment` go over the look's."],[2086,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Toast passes through. `style` goes over the banner's own look."],[2120,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Toggle and ToggleGroup passes through. `style`, `hoverStyle`, `activeStyle`, `focusVisibleStyle`, `pressedStyle` and `disabledStyle` go over the look's."],[2141,"Every prop of `nsh/base` Toolbar, `ToolbarGroup` and `ToolbarSeparator` passes through. `style` goes over the look's. Items keep their own look (`Button`, `Toggle`, …)."],[1818,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through (`style`, `accessibilityLabel`, …); `style` goes over the look's."],[208,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through (`style`, `accessibilityLabel`, `onPress`, …); `style` goes over the look's, so a caller's own width, corners or fill replace the look's and the box keeps its ratio inside them."],[1710,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through (`style`, `role`,\n`accessibilityLabel`, …); `style` goes over the look's."],[1134,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through (`style`, `role`, …); `style` goes over the look's."],[187,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `Alert` and\n`AlertDescription`, and every prop of `nsh` Text on `AlertTitle`;\n`style` goes over the look's on each. The root is `role=\"alert\"`, so a notice is read out when it\nappears."],[306,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `Breadcrumb`,\n`BreadcrumbList`, `BreadcrumbItem`, `BreadcrumbSeparator` and `BreadcrumbEllipsis`, and every prop\nof `nsh` Text on `BreadcrumbPage`; `BreadcrumbLink` is\n`nsh/base`'s Link with all its props (`href`, `openWith`, `onOpen`,\n`onPress`, `disabled`, `hitSlop`, …). Style props go over the look's."],[343,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `BubbleGroup`,\n`Bubble` and `BubbleContent`; `BubbleText` takes every prop of\n`nsh` Text, and `BubbleContent` draws a string child as a\n`BubbleText`. Style props go over the look's."],[916,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `Empty`,\n`EmptyHeader`, `EmptyMedia` and `EmptyContent`, and every prop of\n`nsh` Text on `EmptyTitle` and `EmptyDescription`; `style` goes\nover the look's on each."],[1177,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `Marker` and\n`MarkerIcon` (`role`, `onPress`, `accessibilityLabel`, …), and every prop of\n`nsh` Text on `MarkerContent`. Style props go over the look's:\n`style` on a `View` or `Text` part."],[1334,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `MessageGroup`,\n`Message` and `MessageContent` (`role`, `accessibilityLabel`, `style`, …). With no `children`,\n`MessageAvatar` is this library's `Avatar`: `name`, `src`,\n`fallback`, `onStatusChange` and the rest of its props pass through. With `children` it renders a\n`View` (`style`, `accessibilityLabel` and the other host props still pass through; `name`, `src`\nand the image props are not used). A string child of `MessageFooter` and of `MessageHeader` is\ndrawn as `nsh` Text."],[1287,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on `MessageScroller` and\n`MessageScrollerItem`; `MessageScrollerViewport` takes a `List`'s\n(`keyExtractor`, `estimatedItemSize`, `onViewableItemsChange`, `scrollbar`, …) less the state the\nscroller keeps (`inverted`, `initialScrollIndex`, `initialScrollAtEnd`,\n`maintainVisibleContentPosition`, …), plus `each`, `alignment` and `onLoadMoreAtStart` (all passed to\nthe list — the last one loads older turns) and the child that renders a row; and `MessageScrollerButton` takes this library's\n`Button` props (`variant` defaults to `secondary`, `size` to\n`sm`). `alignment=\"bottom\"` pins a short conversation to the bottom of the viewport. `indicator`\nis a mark at the button's top-end corner (an arrival dot); the arrow stays."],[376,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on all three parts,\nincluding `class` and `classList`. `style` goes over the part's own."],[1113,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on both parts (`style`, `accessibilityLabel`, …); `style` goes over the look's."],[551,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on every part but `CodeBlockTitle` (a `nsh` Text), `CodeBlockCopyButton` (an `IconButton`) and `CodeBlockContent` (a `nsh` Scroll); `style` goes over the look's. The text of the code is selectable."],[2190,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on every part but `TraceTitle` and `TraceDescription` (a `nsh` Text), `TraceCollapsible` (the props below) and `TraceCollapsibleContent` (`nsh/base`'s Collapsible); `style` goes over the look's."],[233,"Every prop of `nsh` View passes through on every part;\n`AttachmentAction` takes this library's `Button` props,\n`AttachmentTrigger` the view's (`onPress`, `accessibilityLabel`, `disabled`, …), and\n`AttachmentTitle`/`AttachmentDescription` the text's. A title or a description is one line,\ntruncated."],[82,"Every registry file the CLI fetches over HTTP is kept in `~/.cache/shadcn-nsh` (`$XDG_CACHE_HOME`, or `SHADCN_NSH_CACHE_DIR` when set). Offline, `diff` compares with those copies and says when they were fetched; the public registry's URL is pinned to the CLI's release, so they are that registry exactly. With no copy, it prints `diff skipped` and exits `2`, so a check can tell \"could not check\" from \"differs\":"],[1645,"Every scroll view"],[37,"Every shadcn-nsh@latest command, with its flags and defaults."],[574,"Every trigger but the `first` draws a divider above it, inside its row, so the hover fill meets the line; `start` lines the trigger and the panel up past a leading icon. A row in the panel (`listRow`) reaches past the content, and the revealed region clips it, so give the panel room on both sides: `panel={{ start: 12, end: 12 }}`."],[952,"Every view prop passes through the parts drawn as views, and every text prop the parts drawn as\ntexts. `style` goes over the look's, so a width or a gap on a part wins."],[1092,"Every view prop passes through the parts drawn as views, and every text prop the parts drawn as\ntexts. `style` goes over the look's."],[99,"Examples"],[122,"Examples"],[164,"Examples"],[197,"Examples"],[216,"Examples"],[253,"Examples"],[276,"Examples"],[294,"Examples"],[325,"Examples"],[361,"Examples"],[386,"Examples"],[442,"Examples"],[457,"Examples"],[483,"Examples"],[509,"Examples"],[528,"Examples"],[566,"Examples"],[584,"Examples"],[607,"Examples"],[630,"Examples"],[664,"Examples"],[685,"Examples"],[706,"Examples"],[728,"Examples"],[748,"Examples"],[782,"Examples"],[802,"Examples"],[821,"Examples"],[849,"Examples"],[876,"Examples"]