()` and the theme take the theme's (Override from `nsh.json`). It is a warning: the command never fails over it, and `add` prints the same line."],[2296,"If the workspace has `apps/web` and a `packages/ui` named `@workspace/ui`:"],[2021,"Images that open"],[973,"ImageViewer"],[1946,"In `nsh-gallery` and `solid-glass`, that is 36 × 20 with a 16-point knob under a pointer and 44 × 24 with 20 on a touch screen (`sm`: 28 × 16 with 12, 36 × 20 with 16): 2 points of track above, below and at each end, so the knob travels its own width — as far from the end on as off."],[1847,"In a button"],[878,"In a composer"],[2253,"In a monorepo, component files live under `packages/ui/` instead of the app root. The theme readers are still `lib/ui/`."],[2308,"In a native menu"],[1921,"In a row"],[1101,"In a sentence"],[537,"In a tool call"],[55,"In an app, `init` also sets up the `@/` import alias the docs' snippets use (`@/components/ui/<name>`, `@/lib/ui/theme`): `tsconfig.json` gains `\"@/*\": [\"./*\"]` under `compilerOptions.paths` — restating the NSH mappings `.nsh/tsconfig.json` declares, because a child's `paths` replace the base's — and `nsh.json` gains `\"resolve\": { \"alias\": { \"@\": \"./\" } }` for `nsh run`/`build`/`test`, which read `nsh.json`, not tsconfig. Values it finds already there are left alone with a warning. A monorepo imports from `@workspace/ui` instead, so it is not touched."],[901,"In the terminal"],[2310,"In the terminal"],[2243,"In this repository, `bun run theme:build` exports three artifacts from the resolved spec. They are generated. Change the TypeScript spec, then run the build. Do not hand-edit the exports and expect the spec to follow."],[1545,"Indeterminate"],[38,"init"],[254,"Initials"],[1161,"Inline"],[2020,"Inline chips"],[1032,"Input"],[989,"InputGroup"],[2317,"Inside a component, the component says how large an icon is and what color it takes, so it matches the label beside it in every variant and state. Spread its glyph helper, or use its 