62,"Use the following composition to build a `TitleBar`:"],[2112,"Use the following composition to build a `Toggle`:"],[2137,"Use the following composition to build a `Toolbar`:"],[2163,"Use the following composition to build a `Tooltip`:"],[2185,"Use the following composition to build a `Trace`:"],[106,"Use the following composition to build an `Accordion`:"],[175,"Use the following composition to build an `Alert`:"],[134,"Use the following composition to build an `AlertDialog`:"],[226,"Use the following composition to build an `Attachment`:"],[261,"Use the following composition to build an `Avatar`:"],[859,"Use the following composition to build an `Editor`:"],[905,"Use the following composition to build an `Empty`:"],[1010,"Use the following composition to build an `InputGroup`:"],[1075,"Use the following composition to build an `Item`:"],[267,"Uses `avatarIdentity` for a named fallback's colors. Every prop of `nsh/base` Avatar passes through on `Avatar`, and every prop of `nsh/base` AvatarGroup on `AvatarGroup` (`limit`, `total`, `overflow`, `overflowAccessibilityLabel`)."],[496,"Uses `carouselArrowLook`, `carouselPaginationLook`, `carouselDotItemLook`, and `CarouselDot`. `carouselArrowLook()`'s `icon` is the glyph an arrow draws and its `style` / `hoverStyle` / `activeStyle` / `focusVisibleStyle` are the arrow's chrome. Every prop of `nsh/base` Carousel parts passes through."],[675,"Uses `commandClasses`, `CommandRow`, `CommandHeading`, and `CommandEmpty` by default. Every prop of `nsh/base` Command passes through."],[722,"Uses `dataTableClasses`. Every prop of `nsh/base` DataTable passes through."],[575,"Uses `disclosureTriggerLook`, `DisclosureChevron`, and `disclosurePanel` from accordion. Composition: `Collapsible`, `CollapsibleTrigger`, `CollapsibleContent`."],[111,"Uses `disclosureTriggerLook`, `DisclosureChevron`, and `disclosurePanel`. Every prop of `nsh/base` Accordion parts passes through."],[1457,"Uses `paginationItemClass` and `paginationArrows` by default. Every prop of `nsh/base` Pagination passes through."],[1484,"Uses `plotCrossLine` and `plotDotClass` by default. Every prop of `nsh/base/plot` Plot passes through."],[1554,"Uses `progressLook`. Every prop of `nsh/base` Progress passes through.\nThe rail is the theme's track form: a sunk groove 6 points high with the inset shade, an accent-tinted\nband 4 points high, or WinUI's 1-point input line under a 3-point run; `height` overrides the height,\nnever the form."],[1650,"Uses `scrollbarTheme` by default. Call `Scrollbar.setTheme()` to install it on every scroll view. Every prop of `nsh/base` Scrollbar passes through."],[1664,"Uses `segmentedLook`. Composition: `Segmented`, `SegmentedList`, `SegmentedItem`. Every prop of `nsh/base` Tabs / `Tab` passes through on the list and items."],[2214,"Uses `TreeRow` by default. Every prop of `nsh/base` Tree passes through."],[1828,"Value column"],[278,"Variant"],[387,"Variant"],[529,"Variant"],[1037,"Variant"],[1066,"Variant"],[2100,"Variant"],[1438,"Verdict"],[1604,"Vertical"],[1829,"Vertical"],[2104,"Vertical"],[2131,"Vertical"],[925,"Vertical and horizontal"],[41,"view"],[2256,"What `theme.json` does not carry is the spec's depth: the eleven `surfaces` (fill, gradient, shadow, edges, material), `feedback` (hover, press, focus, disabled, passive), `controls` (a switch's track, a field's focus line), and `metrics` (sizes per input tier). `add theme-<id>` installs that spec as `themes/<id>.ts`. A field a surface leaves out is a neutral (no gradient, no material, no shadow). A shadow names a step of the theme's own `elevation` scale rather than writing a shadow literal. State a device-dependent size twice, under `pointer` and `touch`, with the same keys."],[4,"What a component file looks like"],[1332,"What a reply carries under it is the app's: a copy that flips to a check for a moment, and two\nthumbs. `IconButton` takes `selected`, so a pressed thumb shows the brand ink and reports\n`accessibilityState={{ selected: true }}`; the rating itself is only the app's state until the app\nsends it."],[1394,"What a trigger opens"],[2231,"What the build writes"],[2298,"When developing this repository:"],[1003,"When to use a group, and when an `Input`"],[863,"Where the bar is and whether it is open are the app's: it sits beside the editor in the same `View`\nrather than inside it, since a part cannot leave the tree. The keys are the app's too — Escape and\n`mod+f` belong to its `keymap`, as a part that captured them would take them from the editor while\nthe bar is closed. Because the search is one object, a query the app sets — from\n`onFindWithSelection`, or from a keybinding — reads in the bar, and the bar's edits move the\neditor's matches as it types."],[1925,"Where the numbers come from"],[1873,"Where the window is horizontally compact, one column shows: the first that `columnVisibility` includes. A choice that should bring the next column in front sets `\"doubleColumn\"`, then `\"detailOnly\"`. The way back is the page's — a button in `leading`, since a desktop has no system back between columns."],[7,"Where to go next"],[1018,"While a reply streams, the send button becomes a stop: the same press that sent the message stops\nthe answer. The plus turns a quarter as the menu under it opens, so the same button shows it can be\nclosed."],[749,"Width"],[2065,"Windows' and Linux's buttons are cells at the trailing end of the bar, filling its height.\nThey sit flush against the window's corner, so the inner content row's trailing padding goes to\nzero while keeping `TitleBar`'s own automatic window-control inset intact:"],[2390,"Windows' Mica is not a surface: it is the window's own `backdrop` in `nsh-desktop` (Windows 11 maps it to Mica or Acrylic, macOS to a visual effect material), set once by the app in `nsh.json` and shown through surfaces whose fill is translucent:"],[2505,"WinUI 3"],[2506,"WinUI 3 (Windows 11): WinUI fill and stroke tokens, 4/8-point circular corners, Segoe UI Variable, Consolas, double focus rings, and timing motion."],[2255,"With `nshm` the same values are `import { colors, control, shape } from \"shadcn-nsh/theme\"`."],[2223,"With `nshm`, import from `shadcn-nsh/<name>`. With the CLI, the file is copied into the app and the snippets on each page import from `@/components/ui/<name>`."],[458,"With a form"],[1495,"With a header"],[1688,"With a pointer the trigger asks for 180 points at least (room for the list's rows). A `width` on\n`style` is the trigger's size and wins over that floor, so `style={{ width: 120 }}` stays 120\npoints inside its parent. `minWidth: 0` still lets a narrow row squeeze a trigger that has no\nwidth of its own, and its title ends in an ellipsis instead of overflowing."],[364,"With a separator"],[365,"With a text addon"],[391,"With an icon"],[165,"With an icon and a note"],[1935,"With no children the track is all of it; a touch screen raises the target to 44 points, and the track\nis already at least that wide, so the hit slop only fills the height."],[1380,"With nothing to lose (`popOnBack` true) the same back press pops without the alert, so the guard\ndisappears the moment the text does."],[2240,"With the CLI, the same call lives in a file the app owns. `npx shadcn-nsh@latest add theme-shadcn` writes `themes/shadcn.ts` plus `themes/shadcn/theme.json` and `DESIGN.md`, beside the build-time theme. Import that module and pass it to `selectTheme`. `init --theme <id>` builds the app on that theme instead. See Themes."],[898,"With what the reader can do"],[2093,"Without `children`, `Toast` draws `title` and `description`. An action and a close button are `toast`'s `action` and `closeButton`."],[640,"Without `multiple`, `value` is the chosen item or `null` (`string | null`). With `multiple`, it is the chosen items (`string[]`)."],[448,"Without `value` the calendar keeps its own, starting at `defaultValue`."],[738,"Without a value the trigger shows `placeholder` (default \"Pick a date\") muted."],[78,"Without an item it lists the installed items that differ; with one it prints the changed lines. `-` is a line of the app's file that overwriting would drop, `+` one it would add. A recolored `theme.json` is not a difference; a missing key is."],[1013,"Write the radius and the padding on the group. The focus ring is drawn on the group's edge, so it follows the radius: a composer on 22 points lights a 22-point ring, with the input and its button inside it."],[48,"Writes `nsh-ui.json`, installs the theme, points every `nsh.json` at it, and sets up the `@/` import alias in an app. Run it once in an app that already has `nsh.json`."],[1357,"Your own header"],[2057,"Your own window controls"]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":0,"2":1,"3":2,"4":3,"5":4,"6":5,"7":6,"8":7,"9":8,"10":9,"11":10,"12":11,"13":12,"14":13,"15":14,"16":15,"17":16,"18":17,"19":18,"20":19,"21":20,"22":21,"23":22,"24":23,"25":24,"26":25,"27":26,"28":27,"29":28,"30":29,"31":30,"32":31,"33":32,"34":33,"35":34,"36":35,"37":36,"38":37,"39":38,"40":39,"41":40,"42":41,"43":42,"44":43,"45":44,"46":45,"47":46,"48":47,"49":48,"50":49,"51":50,"52":51,"53":52,"54":53,"55":54,"56":55,"57":56,"58":57,"59":58,"60":59,"61":60,"62":61,"63":62,"64":63,"65":64,"66":65,"67":66,"68":67,"69":68,"70":69,"71":70,"72":71,"73":72,"74":73,"75":74,"76":75,"77":76,"78":77,"79":78,"80":79,"81":80,"82":81,"83":82,"84":83,"85":84,"86":85,"87":86,"88":87,"89":88,"90":89,"91":90,"92":91,"93":92,"94":103,"95":104,"96":105,"97":106,"98":107,"99":108,"100":109,"101":110,"102":111,"103":112,"104":113,"105":114,"106":115,"107":116,"108":117,"109":118,"110":119,"111":120,"112":121,"113":122,"114":123,"115":124,"116":125,"117":160,"118":161,"119":162,"120":163,"121":164,"122":165,"123":166,"124":167,"125":168,"126":169,"127":170,"128":171,"129":172,"130":173,"131":174,"132":175,"133":176,"134":177,"135":178,"136":179,"137":180,"138":181,"139":182,"140":183,"141":184,"142":185,"143":186,"144":187,"145":188,"146":189,"147":190,"148":191,"1